-- title:
--   Coefficients of the diagonal polynomial of a symmetric form
-- statement:
--   A symmetric $j$-linear form $F$ on $K^r$ is given by coefficients $F(s)$ on multisets $s$ of size $j$, and evaluates as $F(v_1,\dots,v_j)=\sum_{a}F(\mathrm{sym}(a))\prod_iv_i(a_i)$ over all tuples $a:\{1..j\}\to\{1..r\}$, where $\mathrm{sym}(a)$ is the multiset of entries. Let $P_F=\sum_bF(\mathrm{sym}(b))\prod_{j\le h}X_{b_j}$ be the diagonal polynomial of a form of degree $h$. Let $m(s)$ be the number of tuples with multiset $s$, and $X^s$ the monomial with exponent vector $s$. Then
--   $$
--   [X^s]\,P_F=m(s)\,F(s) .
--   $$
--
--   The diagonal polynomial records each coefficient with its multinomial multiplicity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/MetricEntropy/FormPolynomials.lean#L126-L143

